October 18th, 1774

It’s done.

Bart’s plan worked better than any of us could’ve dreamed. The fake Rock Ridge, the replica buildings, 
the cardboard townsfolk — all of it. And wouldn’t you know it, they fell for the whole damn thing.

Taggart and his goons rolled in just past noon, raising hell like they always do — only this time, they weren’t 
destroying Rock Ridge. They were destroying set pieces.

By the time they realized something was off, it was too late. The real townsfolk were hiding behind the hills 
with rifles and dynamite, and once the ambush was sprung, the fight didn’t last long.

Highlight of the day? Taggart screaming about the toll booth we dropped in the middle of the desert trail. 
He actually turned around, stormed off, and came back ten minutes later with “a shit-load of dimes.”

Mongo laughed so hard he dislocated something.

We won’t pretend everything’s perfect. The town’s still got scars. But for once, we’re the ones holding the cards.

And Bart? He just tipped his hat, rode off, and said, “Where I’m headed, the sun’s always setting just right.”

I think he’s earned the ride.

- Jim “The Waco Kid”
